        <mxCell id="LWD75c4iQzc9Z1IKKLG1-15" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 17px;&quot;&gt;The Blueberry Bloom app will implements CRUD functionality to support user interaction and data management. &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;215&quot; data-start=&quot;205&quot;&gt;Creating&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;operations that allow my users to begin new Pomodoro sessions and log new learning chunks. Users can &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;317&quot; data-start=&quot;309&quot;&gt;Read&lt;/strong&gt; motivational quotes, progress in their blueberry garden, and review their brain map of learned material. They can &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;442&quot; data-start=&quot;432&quot;&gt;Update&lt;/strong&gt; their personal goals, learning chunk notes, or reschedule review intervals to use spaced repetition. Finally, users may &lt;strong style=&quot;&quot; data-end=&quot;574&quot; data-start=&quot;564&quot;&gt;Delete&lt;/strong&gt; completed tasks, outdated chunks, or reset parts of their garden to refresh their learning focus. These CRUD operations ensure the app remains flexible, personalized, and engaging for neurodivergent learner&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="10" width="940" height="340" as="geometry" />
